1. DEFINITIONS

"Project" means the original Living Planet («Живая планета») software and
its original accompanying source code, documentation, and assets that
TPECKA180 owns or is authorized to license under these terms.

"Covered Material" means the Project and any modifications or derivative
works incorporating copyright-protected portions of the Project, but not
independent works or separately licensed third-party material.

"Modified Version" means a version of Covered Material that has been
changed, extended, translated, adapted, or combined with other work.

"Distribution" includes making copies, downloads, installations, or
hosted access available to others.

"Corresponding Source" means the editable source code, scripts, assets,
build instructions, and modifications reasonably needed to build and
modify the Covered Material, excluding separately licensed dependencies
that can be obtained independently.

2. PERMISSION TO USE AND IMPROVE

Subject to all conditions below, each recipient receives a worldwide,
non-exclusive, royalty-free permission, for the duration of the applicable
copyright, to use, study, copy, modify, and distribute Covered Material
and Modified Versions.

Private modifications do not have to be published. No copyright or
ownership in the original Project is transferred to recipients.

3. THE GAME AND ITS MODIFICATIONS MUST REMAIN FREE OF CHARGE

No person may sell, rent, license for a fee, or impose any mandatory
payment for downloading, obtaining, playing, using, copying, updating,
or accessing Covered Material or a Modified Version.

This prohibits paywalls, paid builds, paid DLC derived from Covered
Material, subscriptions required for access, in-game purchases,
microtransactions, paid gameplay features, and monetization through
advertisements embedded in a distributed Modified Version.

Distribution and access to Covered Material must remain free of charge,
including when bundled with other software or hosted online. A
distributor may not disguise a required payment as a processing,
delivery, activation, or support fee.

Unconditional, voluntary donations are allowed only if contributors
and non-contributors receive the same full free access, functionality,
updates, and source code; donations must not unlock content or features.

These restrictions concern Covered Material. They do not prohibit
independent works that do not incorporate protected Project material.

4. SOURCE AVAILABILITY AND SAME-LICENSE DISTRIBUTION

When distributing any Covered Material or Modified Version, you must:

(a) Provide the complete Corresponding Source without charge, either
    with the distribution or through a conspicuous, functioning,
    publicly accessible link available without registration or payment.
(b) License all original-project-derived portions and your copyrightable
    modifications to those portions under this same Version 1.0, so that
    every subsequent recipient receives the permissions and obligations
    stated here. Contributors retain copyright in their own additions.
(c) Include this LICENSE text unmodified with the distributed Covered
    Material, and preserve all existing legally required third-party
    notices and licenses.
(d) Clearly identify material changes and the contributors responsible
    for them, without implying that the original creator endorsed them.
(e) Not impose extra licensing, technical, or contractual restrictions
    that prevent recipients from exercising rights granted here.

This section does not purport to relicense independent third-party works.

5. MANDATORY ORIGINAL-CREATOR CREDIT

Every publicly distributed Covered Material or Modified Version must
include a README.md at the top level of its source distribution.

The FIRST visible sentence of that README.md, before any heading,
image, badge, slogan, or other introduction, must be exactly:

Original Living Planet («Живая планета») was created by TPECKA180; original source: https://github.com/TPECKA180/living-planet.

Additional translations, credits, headings, and descriptions may follow
that first sentence, but may not replace or obscure it.

Where the Covered Material is presented or downloaded on a public page,
the original creator and original-repository URL must also be clearly
identified in the page's description or credits.

Every playable Modified Version with a graphical or text user interface
must display "Original creator: TPECKA180" and
"https://github.com/TPECKA180/living-planet" in a reasonably accessible,
readable "About", "Credits", or equivalent section. The credit must not
be concealed or misrepresented. If such a section does not exist, one
must be provided for distributed playable Modified Versions.

Do not remove existing notices of copyright, original authorship, or
this license. Other contributors may receive prominent credit for their
own work, but may not claim to be the creator of the original Project.

